# 351-KRN-0166 — The loader's handoff versioned apart from the system-call ABI — done

**Type:** kernel (`main.rs`), `common/abi.rs`, bootloader · **Owner:** kernel session · **Priority:** P1 · **Status:** done (2026-10-23) · **Blocked by:** — · **Main task:** [351](../issues/351-self-update.md) · **Constitution:** MC-12.4, MC-12.7, MC-6.5

From EFF's request of 2026-10-23 (`internal-dev-messages`, `KRN/2026-10-23T1856Z-EFF-two-requests-a-slot-update-across-a-syscall-abi-change.md`), filed at the maintainer's word.

## Problem

- **One number covers two interfaces.** `BootInfo.abi_version` carries the system-call ABI (`ABI_VERSION`). The kernel compares it with its own at its first instruction and stops on any difference (`kernel/src/main.rs`).
- **Two ABIs that left the handoff alone still needed a new stick.**
  - ABI 18 added `WORKER_START`; ABI 19, large pages and `ALLOC_SMALL_PAGES`. Neither changed `BootInfo`.
  - Yet a kernel of either refuses the ABI 17 loader.
  - A machine whose `BOOTX64.EFI` lies outside its slots therefore cannot take such a kernel through a slot update; the MacBook Pro over the link is one.
- **Programs already check the right thing.** `libmind` compares a program's ABI with the kernel's (`libmind/src/process.rs`). The loader's check is the one that is too wide.

## Plan

1. **Two versions in `common/abi.rs`.**
   - `ABI_VERSION`, as now, between programs and the kernel.
   - `BOOT_HANDOFF_VERSION`, for `BootInfo`'s layout and meaning between the loader and the kernel.
2. **The field at offset 720 holds the handoff version.**
   - The loader writes `BOOT_HANDOFF_VERSION` there.
   - The kernel accepts the versions whose `BootInfo` it reads as its own: from the ABI at which `BootInfo` last changed up to `BOOT_HANDOFF_VERSION`.
   - Older loaders wrote their ABI there, so an ABI 17 loader is accepted when `BootInfo` has not changed since 17. Which ABI that is, is found by comparing `BootInfo` across the ABI notes in `common/abi.rs`.
3. **A change to `BootInfo` raises `BOOT_HANDOFF_VERSION`** and moves the lowest accepted version to it. That is the explicit transition of MC-12.4: a kernel and a loader of different handoffs refuse each other, with the message they give now.
4. **A host test pins the layout**: `BootInfo`'s size and its fields' offsets. A layout change without a new handoff version fails it.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] A kernel of ABI 19 boots from the loader of an earlier ABI whose `BootInfo` is the same (QEMU, x86 and aarch64), and programs of ABI 19 run.
- [x] A loader of another handoff is refused with the message, as now, by the test kernel the `loader-abi-test` feature builds.
- [x] Host tests: the layout pinned; the accepted range named in one place.
- [x] `docs/api` and `docs/profile` state the two versions and which change needs a new loader.

## Progress (2026-10-23)

Made on `claude/youthful-mendel-mf1soy` (585331ac):
- **`common/abi.rs`:** `BOOT_HANDOFF_VERSION` (19), `BOOT_HANDOFF_OLDEST` (16) and `handoff_accepted`.
- **Where the handoff last changed.** `BootInfo`, `BOOT_FILES` and its constants are the same since ABI 16's two Effector images (750-KRN-0119, dc5e6dcd), and `bootloader/` has no commit since. ABI 15 had 41 images.
- **The loader** writes the handoff version.
- **The kernel** takes 16 to 19. Its message names the range: `KERNEL STOPPED: THE BOOTLOADER HANDS OVER VERSION n, THIS KERNEL TAKES a TO b`.
- **The `loader-abi-test` kernel** takes only 20.
- **Checked** (this session's container, QEMU TCG):
  - host test `the_handoff_takes_every_loader_since_abi_16_and_no_other`: `BootInfo` is 1048 bytes, 43 images, the range 16 to 19;
  - the x86 `boot` suite: the test kernel refuses the loader with the new message, on COM1 and on the screen; the trial boots pass;
  - `tests/aarch64_smoke.py`: the boot and the trial slots;
  - **today's kernel and programs from the loader of ABI 17,** built from `main` 344aa298: the `shell` suite on x86 and on aarch64. These are one run each, outside the gate, and that loader is not kept as a fixture.
- **What it gives the MacBook.** Its stick's loader (ABI 17) takes kernels of ABI 17 to 19, and later ones until `BootInfo` changes. EFF's stick needs no rewrite for these.

## Resolution

Landed in round 26 (`main` 6bf90421, 2026-10-23); every gate group passed on that commit, i9's on rz-2 while i9 was out (QEMU, x86 and aarch64).
- **What was made.** `BOOT_HANDOFF_VERSION` (19) and `BOOT_HANDOFF_OLDEST` (16) live in `common/abi.rs`; the loader writes the handoff version in the word at offset 720.
  - The kernel takes 16 to 19, because `BootInfo` and the boot images have not changed since ABI 16.
  - The `loader-abi-test` kernel takes only 20.
  - The host test `boot_abi` pins `BootInfo`'s size (1048 bytes), the image count (43) and the range.
- **Docs.** `docs/api` and `docs/profile` (the MC-11.1 row) say which change needs a new loader.
- **Evidence outside the gate.** Today's kernel and programs booted from the loader of ABI 17 (`main` 344aa298): one run of the `shell` suite on x86 and one on aarch64.
- **What it gives the MacBook.** Its stick's loader (ABI 17) takes kernels of ABI 17 to 19, and later ones until `BootInfo` changes. A slot update across these ABIs needs no new stick.
- **Not tried:** the MacBook itself.

